From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:58:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Games] Fix an empty leaderboard after submitting a score

A submission tells the standings dialog to rebuild even while it is
closed. With no leaderboard chosen, that sets "The standings could not
be loaded", and the skin hides the list while a status is set. The next
time the dialog opens, its list is left out of the view control because
it is hidden at that moment, so the rows that arrive a second later are
never bound and the dialog shows an empty table.

Ignore the refresh while the dialog is closed. It builds its list when
it opens anyway.
---
 xbmc/games/dialogs/osd/DialogGameLeaderboardEntries.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/games/dialogs/osd/DialogGameLeaderboardEntries.cpp b/xbmc/games/dialogs/osd/DialogGameLeaderboardEntries.cpp
index f42dbe8..38082c2 100644
--- a/xbmc/games/dialogs/osd/DialogGameLeaderboardEntries.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/games/dialogs/osd/DialogGameLeaderboardEntries.cpp
@@ -357,6 +357,11 @@ bool CDialogGameLeaderboardEntries::OnMessage(CGUIMessage& message)
 {
   if (message.GetMessage() == GUI_MSG_NOTIFY_ALL && message.GetParam1() == GUI_MSG_REFRESH_LIST)
   {
+    // A status set while closed would hide the list when the dialog next opens,
+    // and a list hidden then is never given its rows
+    if (!IsActive())
+      return true;
+
     PopulateList();
 
     // Only when something dropped the page. A refresh that follows a fetch of
